From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iasnezhkov <iasnezhkov@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:57:03 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] mindone: SignApk falls back when conscrypt cannot load

The tree builds with a native aarch64 JDK (its own x86-64 JDK crashes
under Rosetta), and the conscrypt host JNI library exists for x86-64
only. Security.insertProviderAt(new OpenSSLProvider(), 1) then throws
UnsatisfiedLinkError and every APK signing step, and with it the build,
fails. Conscrypt is only a speed optimisation here: on failure SignApk
logs it and continues with Bouncy Castle and the JDK providers, which
sign correctly.

Change-Id: I3872c7839c9d886d9ab666829e113039710cc0b8
---
 tools/signapk/src/com/android/signapk/SignApk.java | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/signapk/src/com/android/signapk/SignApk.java b/tools/signapk/src/com/android/signapk/SignApk.java
index 654e19675d..f31f39f082 100644
--- a/tools/signapk/src/com/android/signapk/SignApk.java
+++ b/tools/signapk/src/com/android/signapk/SignApk.java
@@ -1076,7 +1076,12 @@ class SignApk {
 
         // Install Conscrypt as the highest-priority provider. Its crypto primitives are faster than
         // the standard or Bouncy Castle ones.
-        Security.insertProviderAt(new OpenSSLProvider(), 1);
+        try {
+            Security.insertProviderAt(new OpenSSLProvider(), 1);
+        } catch (Throwable t) {
+            System.err.println("SignApk: conscrypt unavailable (" + t
+                    + "); using Bouncy Castle / JDK providers");
+        }
         // Install Bouncy Castle (as the lowest-priority provider) because Conscrypt does not offer
         // DSA which may still be needed.
         // TODO: Stop installing Bouncy Castle provider once DSA is no longer needed.
